1
00:00:12,600 --> 00:00:14,440
(18+ viewers only)

2
00:00:14,440 --> 00:00:15,960
(18+ viewers only
May contain disturbing content)

3
00:00:15,960 --> 00:00:17,120
(Contains violence, sex,
and strong language)

4
00:00:17,400 --> 00:00:18,720
(This series is a work of fiction and is not related to any actual person, place, organization, or event.)

5
00:00:18,720 --> 00:00:21,120
(During the production process, AI technology was used in certain scenes to support on-set safety, )

6
00:00:21,120 --> 00:00:23,000
(as well as to enhance the quality and realism of the visual presentation.)

7
00:00:25,080 --> 00:00:26,280
(Do you know?)

8
00:00:27,400 --> 00:00:29,680
(Do you know what's worse than death?)

9
00:00:31,560 --> 00:00:34,080
(It's opening your eyes)

10
00:00:34,400 --> 00:00:35,960
(and finding yourself still breathing,)

11
00:00:36,880 --> 00:00:39,160
(even though 200 years ago,)

12
00:00:39,160 --> 00:00:41,720
(you begged for it to stop.)

13
00:00:42,880 --> 00:00:43,640
(1821 AD, 4th Death)

14
00:00:43,640 --> 00:00:45,120
(I thought the flames)

15
00:00:45,840 --> 00:00:48,280
(would burn everything away.)

16
00:00:50,600 --> 00:00:53,000
(Why is this body so stubborn,)

17
00:00:55,600 --> 00:00:58,040
(forcing me)

18
00:00:58,360 --> 00:01:00,080
(to open my eyes again?)

19
00:01:04,400 --> 00:01:06,240
(Now that the fire rejected me,)

20
00:01:06,960 --> 00:01:08,840
(perhaps water was the next answer.)

21
00:01:09,320 --> 00:01:10,560
(1837 AD, 69th Death)

22
00:01:10,560 --> 00:01:12,600
(Everything in this world)

23
00:01:12,760 --> 00:01:14,680
(must eventually reach its end.)

24
00:01:15,440 --> 00:01:18,600
(All rivers eventually meet the sea,)

25
00:01:19,160 --> 00:01:21,240
(just as all things end in death.)

26
00:01:21,760 --> 00:01:24,000
(I thought the ocean would show mercy)

27
00:01:26,200 --> 00:01:29,640
(and let my body sink to the bottom.)

28
00:01:31,200 --> 00:01:32,200
(One day.)

29
00:01:32,800 --> 00:01:33,880
(One night.)

30
00:01:35,400 --> 00:01:37,080
(I endured the agony of suffocation.)

31
00:01:39,440 --> 00:01:40,960
(Only then did I realize)

32
00:01:43,200 --> 00:01:45,960
(the ocean had rejected me too.)

33
00:01:47,240 --> 00:01:49,920
(1914 AD, 101st Death)

34
00:01:49,920 --> 00:01:51,680
(Humans had grown smarter.)

35
00:01:52,200 --> 00:01:55,600
(They invented faster ways to kill.)

36
00:01:56,480 --> 00:01:59,600
(The darkness I longed for)

37
00:01:59,600 --> 00:02:00,800
(finally answered me.)

38
00:02:07,560 --> 00:02:10,440
(But bullets that took countless lives)

39
00:02:11,800 --> 00:02:15,120
(gave me only a fleeting dream.)

40
00:02:26,680 --> 00:02:27,440
(1987 AD, 168th Death)

41
00:02:27,440 --> 00:02:29,560
(I love the music of this era.)

42
00:02:30,920 --> 00:02:32,680
(It makes me feel)

43
00:02:33,120 --> 00:02:34,880
(a little more alive.)

44
00:02:36,320 --> 00:02:37,160
(Humans)

45
00:02:38,600 --> 00:02:41,440
(escape reality
through music and booze.)

46
00:02:42,280 --> 00:02:44,160
(They drink themselves senseless)

47
00:02:44,720 --> 00:02:47,320
(to forget their pain for one night.)

48
00:02:47,680 --> 00:02:50,840
(But alcohol can never intoxicate me,)

49
00:02:51,040 --> 00:02:53,080
(no matter how much I drink.)

50
00:02:55,640 --> 00:02:57,360
(Since I can't get drunk,)

51
00:02:59,080 --> 00:03:01,280
(I might as well find a way to die.)

52
00:03:01,280 --> 00:03:02,520
I'm going out for a smoke.

53
00:03:07,360 --> 00:03:08,920
Your face is hilarious.

54
00:03:10,240 --> 00:03:10,920
Hmph.

55
00:03:11,320 --> 00:03:13,120
Is my face funny?

56
00:03:13,120 --> 00:03:14,000
Huh?

57
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:18,760
Is my face funny?

58
00:03:18,760 --> 00:03:19,680
Uncle!

59
00:03:19,680 --> 00:03:24,320
Enough! That's enough!

60
00:03:24,320 --> 00:03:25,520
You want to fight me?

61
00:03:25,520 --> 00:03:27,280
Ken!

62
00:03:29,480 --> 00:03:33,200
(In 1997,
the Asian financial crisis hit.)

63
00:03:33,200 --> 00:03:36,480
(Everything collapsed in an instant.)

64
00:03:37,280 --> 00:03:39,880
(1998 AD, 178th Death)

65
00:03:39,880 --> 00:03:41,440
(In a capitalist world,)

66
00:03:42,280 --> 00:03:44,360
(people leaped from high-rises)

67
00:03:44,960 --> 00:03:46,360
(to escape reality.)

68
00:03:55,160 --> 00:03:56,640
(But to me,)

69
00:03:57,520 --> 00:03:59,160
(they were still fortunate.)

70
00:04:00,360 --> 00:04:02,360
(At least death welcomed them.)

71
00:04:03,240 --> 00:04:04,600
(But me?)

72
00:04:05,120 --> 00:04:07,000
(No matter how the world collapses,)

73
00:04:07,280 --> 00:04:10,360
(this body forces me to adapt)

74
00:04:10,360 --> 00:04:12,000
(and keep living.)

75
00:04:15,720 --> 00:04:18,880
(2021 AD, 235th Death)

76
00:04:34,960 --> 00:04:36,640
(Wash, Dry, Iron)

77
00:04:42,840 --> 00:04:43,840
(Ken.)

78
00:04:47,600 --> 00:04:48,680
(It wasn't until later)

79
00:04:49,560 --> 00:04:50,840
(that I learned)

80
00:04:51,040 --> 00:04:54,200
(someone could kill Nours like us.)

81
00:04:58,520 --> 00:04:59,840
(And now,)

82
00:05:00,960 --> 00:05:03,320
(death is my only goal.)

83
00:05:09,280 --> 00:05:13,760
=Nour=
(A WeTV Original Series)

84
00:05:15,520 --> 00:05:17,920
(Five Years Later, B.E. 2569)
A charred body was found

85
00:05:17,920 --> 00:05:19,480
found on a waste field.

86
00:05:19,480 --> 00:05:20,360
The M.O.

87
00:05:20,360 --> 00:05:23,000
(Nakhon Sawan Province)
matches that of several recent murders.

88
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:24,840
The killer was still at large.

89
00:05:24,840 --> 00:05:26,280
Rumors spread through the area.

90
00:05:26,280 --> 00:05:27,880
Many residents claimed

91
00:05:27,880 --> 00:05:29,760
the Nours might be behind the murders.

92
00:05:46,920 --> 00:05:52,040
=Episode 1=
(The Red Line)

93
00:05:52,040 --> 00:05:53,200
Easy, man.

94
00:05:53,200 --> 00:05:55,120
Put the weapon down, okay?

95
00:05:55,400 --> 00:05:56,240
No!

96
00:05:56,920 --> 00:05:58,440
I didn't kill my wife!

97
00:05:58,800 --> 00:06:01,480
He burned his wife in their home.
He's insane.

98
00:06:01,480 --> 00:06:02,480
He's a demon.

99
00:06:02,480 --> 00:06:04,360
Is he high out of his mind
or possessed by a Nour?

100
00:06:04,360 --> 00:06:05,320
Stay back!

101
00:06:05,320 --> 00:06:06,520
Easy, man.

102
00:06:06,520 --> 00:06:08,080
Put the weapon down slowly.

103
00:06:08,080 --> 00:06:09,320
We can talk this out.

104
00:06:09,320 --> 00:06:10,680
No. There's nothing to discuss.

105
00:06:10,680 --> 00:06:11,320
Go!

106
00:06:22,880 --> 00:06:23,720
Hey!

107
00:06:23,720 --> 00:06:24,400
Ow!

108
00:06:25,080 --> 00:06:25,760
Hey!

109
00:06:25,760 --> 00:06:26,720
Watch out!

110
00:06:27,480 --> 00:06:28,520
Hey!

111
00:06:41,040 --> 00:06:43,120
- Sergeant, lend me your cuffs.
- The cuffs?

112
00:06:43,120 --> 00:06:44,200
Who is that?

113
00:06:44,200 --> 00:06:45,960
All right, show's over. Go home.

114
00:06:45,960 --> 00:06:47,040
Please make way.

115
00:06:47,040 --> 00:06:48,080
Move along.

116
00:06:48,080 --> 00:06:48,800
What the hell?

117
00:06:48,800 --> 00:06:50,200
Back up! Everyone, back up!

118
00:06:50,200 --> 00:06:51,200
Go!

119
00:06:52,480 --> 00:06:53,880
Tangme, are you okay?

120
00:06:53,880 --> 00:06:54,480
Phong.

121
00:06:54,480 --> 00:06:54,960
Yeah?

122
00:06:54,960 --> 00:06:56,200
Thank God you're safe.

123
00:06:56,200 --> 00:06:57,760
The Special Investigation Unit
saved you.

124
00:06:58,080 --> 00:06:59,040
Special Investigation Unit?

125
00:06:59,040 --> 00:07:00,480
It's Inspector James.

126
00:07:00,480 --> 00:07:02,240
He transferred here this morning.

127
00:07:02,240 --> 00:07:03,480
No way. That's Inspector James?

128
00:07:03,480 --> 00:07:04,160
Yeah.

129
00:07:04,160 --> 00:07:05,640
The daredevil who took down that gang?

130
00:07:05,640 --> 00:07:06,160
Yeah.

131
00:07:06,160 --> 00:07:08,760
There were over a dozen criminals.

132
00:07:08,760 --> 00:07:11,560
Inspector James drove them off alone.

133
00:07:11,560 --> 00:07:14,080
I'd run too. Who could take him on?

134
00:07:14,080 --> 00:07:14,840
True.

135
00:07:14,840 --> 00:07:17,400
If he keeps going this hard,
what'll happen to our station?

136
00:07:17,400 --> 00:07:19,600
(Nakhon Sawan Provincial Police Station
Jan 8, 2026, 10:00 a.m.)

137
00:07:31,840 --> 00:07:33,920
Well, if it isn't the famous
Inspector James.

138
00:07:34,160 --> 00:07:35,520
Welcome.

139
00:07:35,760 --> 00:07:36,840
(CID)
I'm Officer Phong.

140
00:07:36,840 --> 00:07:38,800
Just call me Phong. I don't mind.

141
00:07:39,360 --> 00:07:42,520
I'm James, Special Investigation Unit 6.

142
00:07:42,520 --> 00:07:45,200
I'm here to take over
the serial arson murders.

143
00:07:45,640 --> 00:07:48,280
Please hand over all related evidence.

144
00:07:48,280 --> 00:07:48,960
Sure.

145
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:50,840
(CID)

146
00:07:50,880 --> 00:07:51,600
Yai.

147
00:07:51,600 --> 00:07:52,120
Yes?

148
00:07:52,720 --> 00:07:53,760
Bring the files.

149
00:07:53,760 --> 00:07:54,400
Sure.

150
00:07:56,920 --> 00:07:58,560
All the files are here.

151
00:07:59,240 --> 00:08:01,360
Key evidence went to headquarters.

152
00:08:01,840 --> 00:08:03,760
They stopped investigating long ago.

153
00:08:04,080 --> 00:08:06,080
Everyone knows no human did this.

154
00:08:06,960 --> 00:08:08,240
It was the Nour ghost.

155
00:08:09,760 --> 00:08:10,640
The Nour ghost?

156
00:08:10,640 --> 00:08:11,440
Yes.

157
00:08:11,440 --> 00:08:12,440
The Nour ghost.

158
00:08:12,440 --> 00:08:14,160
Not just Joe from this morning.

159
00:08:14,160 --> 00:08:15,920
Every officer who investigated this case

160
00:08:15,920 --> 00:08:17,480
knows the Nour ghost did it.

161
00:08:18,400 --> 00:08:20,160
It's terrifying.

162
00:08:20,920 --> 00:08:23,800
It has blue eyes and fangs.

163
00:08:26,560 --> 00:08:28,720
Do you blame everything here
on the Nour ghost?

164
00:08:29,720 --> 00:08:30,800
Inspector.

165
00:08:30,800 --> 00:08:33,680
You came here for this minor case?

166
00:08:34,280 --> 00:08:36,640
I'm here on orders from
National Police Headquarters

167
00:08:36,640 --> 00:08:39,000
to investigate the unsolved arson cases.

168
00:08:42,400 --> 00:08:44,680
But after seeing how you work,

169
00:08:45,440 --> 00:08:47,200
I'm not surprised it's still unsolved.

170
00:08:48,400 --> 00:08:50,360
Forget it. I'll show you your office.

171
00:08:50,880 --> 00:08:51,720
Come on.

172
00:08:54,240 --> 00:08:55,320
This way.

173
00:08:59,040 --> 00:09:00,280
There's so much dust.

174
00:09:00,480 --> 00:09:02,280
Why is this station such a mess?

175
00:09:08,480 --> 00:09:09,920
This is my desk, right?

176
00:09:13,520 --> 00:09:14,920
What are you doing?

177
00:09:16,800 --> 00:09:18,160
This desk belonged to your predecessor.

178
00:09:18,160 --> 00:09:19,480
Why keep his nameplate?

179
00:09:19,480 --> 00:09:22,040
No, your desk is here.
Don't touch that one.

180
00:09:22,280 --> 00:09:23,800
That's Inspector Ken's desk.

181
00:09:23,800 --> 00:09:26,000
Inspector Ken

182
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:27,960
is handling Joe's case too?

183
00:09:28,720 --> 00:09:30,720
Yeah, just like you.

184
00:09:31,280 --> 00:09:34,040
He knows Joe did it,
yet he keeps investigating.

185
00:09:34,600 --> 00:09:36,760
The police dropped the case long ago.

186
00:09:36,760 --> 00:09:38,040
They all know the Nour ghost did it.

187
00:09:38,760 --> 00:09:41,400
But you can't put a ghost in prison,

188
00:09:41,720 --> 00:09:43,400
so someone has to take the fall.

189
00:09:44,360 --> 00:09:45,840
Where is he now?

190
00:09:46,240 --> 00:09:47,840
I'd like to say hello.

191
00:09:49,520 --> 00:09:51,240
Hmm.

192
00:09:53,360 --> 00:09:54,400
Inspector.

193
00:09:55,760 --> 00:09:59,040
Easy information comes at a price.

194
00:10:00,840 --> 00:10:01,720
Hey.

195
00:10:04,720 --> 00:10:05,880
I don't have cash.

196
00:10:08,920 --> 00:10:10,240
Use the QR code.

197
00:10:10,400 --> 00:10:11,440
I'll scan it.

198
00:10:11,440 --> 00:10:12,200
Hey!

199
00:10:13,040 --> 00:10:14,040
Inspector.

200
00:10:14,600 --> 00:10:17,680
(Nakhon Sawan Provincial Hospital
Jan 8, 2026, 01:40 p.m.)

201
00:10:17,680 --> 00:10:19,520
Special Investigation Unit.

202
00:10:19,520 --> 00:10:20,200
(Superintendent Kiran)

203
00:10:20,200 --> 00:10:22,360
And you're a forensic pathologist?

204
00:10:22,360 --> 00:10:25,640
Number 157.

205
00:10:47,160 --> 00:10:49,040
(Forensic Medicine)

206
00:11:11,560 --> 00:11:12,440
Doctor.

207
00:11:14,080 --> 00:11:16,280
The victim died the same way
as the previous ones.

208
00:11:16,880 --> 00:11:20,040
How long do I have to keep
this a secret?

209
00:11:20,040 --> 00:11:21,800
Until we find the killer.

210
00:11:22,000 --> 00:11:23,240
Okay.

211
00:11:24,280 --> 00:11:25,680
I'll handle it.

212
00:12:47,120 --> 00:12:48,120
Who are you?

213
00:12:50,640 --> 00:12:52,000
What are you doing here?

214
00:12:52,560 --> 00:12:54,120
I'm with the Special Investigation Unit.

215
00:12:54,120 --> 00:12:55,400
I'm investigating the arson case.

216
00:12:56,080 --> 00:12:57,840
Do you have a warrant?

217
00:12:58,920 --> 00:13:00,560
You can't enter without it.

218
00:13:01,600 --> 00:13:04,120
It'll be delivered shortly.

219
00:13:04,360 --> 00:13:05,920
But for now, please step aside.

220
00:13:05,920 --> 00:13:07,040
I have work to do.

221
00:13:11,560 --> 00:13:12,360
You...

222
00:13:15,240 --> 00:13:17,000
Dr. Jiratikarn.

223
00:13:17,640 --> 00:13:19,360
Are you the forensic pathologist here?

224
00:13:19,520 --> 00:13:20,360
Yes.

225
00:13:20,560 --> 00:13:22,360
Outsiders aren't allowed in here.

226
00:13:22,840 --> 00:13:24,040
Hmm.

227
00:13:24,240 --> 00:13:26,320
Isn't that man an outsider too?

228
00:13:26,400 --> 00:13:27,800
Why is he allowed to stay?

229
00:13:28,240 --> 00:13:30,520
Chita is a rescue worker
I brought in to help me.

230
00:13:30,520 --> 00:13:33,040
I should be asking why you're here.

231
00:13:34,040 --> 00:13:35,440
I'm investigating the case.

232
00:13:35,760 --> 00:13:38,160
Don't worry about the warrant.

233
00:13:38,160 --> 00:13:39,360
It'll arrive shortly.

234
00:13:39,560 --> 00:13:42,720
If you want to come in to investigate,
follow the proper procedure.

235
00:13:42,960 --> 00:13:44,920
And Inspector Ken handles this body.

236
00:13:45,280 --> 00:13:47,640
Fine. I'll notify Inspector Ken.

237
00:13:47,640 --> 00:13:49,400
We're on the same team.

238
00:14:05,280 --> 00:14:06,480
What exactly do you want?

239
00:14:21,400 --> 00:14:22,800
I know who you are.

240
00:14:23,160 --> 00:14:24,400
But please leave.

241
00:14:24,600 --> 00:14:25,960
What's your problem?

242
00:14:25,960 --> 00:14:27,560
We're in the same department.

243
00:14:30,480 --> 00:14:31,720
Wait.

244
00:14:36,240 --> 00:14:38,880
You're Inspector
Kiran Amatanathi, right?

245
00:14:39,640 --> 00:14:41,640
Let's start over.

246
00:14:42,160 --> 00:14:43,160
Hello.

247
00:14:43,400 --> 00:14:46,080
I'm Superintendent Nainet Inthakan.

248
00:14:46,080 --> 00:14:47,480
I transferred from Bangkok

249
00:14:47,480 --> 00:14:49,920
to help with the serial arson murders.

250
00:14:49,920 --> 00:14:52,360
I'd like more information on Joe's case.

251
00:14:52,760 --> 00:14:54,560
I hope you'll cooperate, Inspector.

252
00:15:37,080 --> 00:15:38,200
Getting enough rest?

253
00:15:38,200 --> 00:15:38,800
What?

254
00:15:40,640 --> 00:15:42,200
Your pulse is fast and weak.

255
00:15:42,560 --> 00:15:43,880
Have you been drinking enough water?

256
00:15:44,560 --> 00:15:45,920
Get a medical checkup.

257
00:15:46,080 --> 00:15:47,520
It could be a thyroid problem.

258
00:15:59,760 --> 00:16:01,520
He turned that around on you, huh?

259
00:16:08,120 --> 00:16:09,120
Come on!

260
00:16:09,320 --> 00:16:11,120
It's bad enough he blocked the case.

261
00:16:11,120 --> 00:16:13,120
He even meddled and took my pulse.

262
00:16:13,360 --> 00:16:15,240
He is a doctor, after all.

263
00:16:15,240 --> 00:16:17,880
He didn't even look at me when he spoke.

264
00:16:18,120 --> 00:16:21,120
How can I keep investigating this case?

265
00:16:21,720 --> 00:16:23,720
If you want the files quickly,

266
00:16:23,720 --> 00:16:25,000
there may be a way.

267
00:16:25,840 --> 00:16:26,720
What way?

268
00:16:39,800 --> 00:16:40,840
That's it?

269
00:16:41,880 --> 00:16:42,880
Do you want it or not?

270
00:16:43,800 --> 00:16:45,000
Yes! Yes!

271
00:16:46,800 --> 00:16:49,280
Inspector Ken doesn't trust people.

272
00:16:49,560 --> 00:16:52,120
He keeps every case file
in his own folder.

273
00:16:52,320 --> 00:16:53,800
An old black folder.

274
00:16:53,800 --> 00:16:54,760
A folder?

275
00:16:55,360 --> 00:16:57,720
He still keeps files
in folders these days?

276
00:16:57,720 --> 00:16:59,000
Exactly.

277
00:16:59,840 --> 00:17:01,960
Where is that file now?

278
00:17:03,200 --> 00:17:04,520
No idea.

279
00:17:05,720 --> 00:17:07,600
If it isn't at the station,

280
00:17:07,920 --> 00:17:09,600
he probably has it on him.

281
00:17:10,840 --> 00:17:11,960
He carries it around?

282
00:17:11,960 --> 00:17:12,800
Yeah.

283
00:17:24,080 --> 00:17:25,040
Dr. Ji.

284
00:17:25,040 --> 00:17:25,520
What is it?

285
00:17:25,520 --> 00:17:26,880
Take this case.
I need to grab something.

286
00:17:26,880 --> 00:17:27,480
Sure.

287
00:17:29,480 --> 00:17:31,480
I see. Now I get it.

288
00:17:31,480 --> 00:17:33,400
You weren't in the same academy intake,

289
00:17:33,400 --> 00:17:34,720
but you're in the same unit.

290
00:17:34,720 --> 00:17:36,200
That's right, Doctor.

291
00:17:36,200 --> 00:17:39,160
But I'd never met him before.

292
00:17:40,440 --> 00:17:41,360
Hey.

293
00:17:41,520 --> 00:17:42,880
Ken.

294
00:17:42,880 --> 00:17:45,200
You got a new partner
and didn't tell me?

295
00:17:45,200 --> 00:17:47,040
Why pin him down like that
the other day?

296
00:17:47,040 --> 00:17:48,120
A partner?

297
00:17:48,920 --> 00:17:50,600
Hello, partner.

298
00:17:51,120 --> 00:17:52,960
Inspector James seems very capable.

299
00:17:52,960 --> 00:17:54,800
He should help lighten your workload.

300
00:17:56,320 --> 00:17:57,080
By the way,

301
00:17:57,080 --> 00:17:59,320
I just finished Somying's autopsy.

302
00:17:59,520 --> 00:18:00,920
It's similar to the earlier cases.

303
00:18:00,920 --> 00:18:02,280
For a charred body,

304
00:18:02,280 --> 00:18:05,200
normally the outside would burn
more severely than the inside.

305
00:18:05,440 --> 00:18:08,600
But this body was almost
completely charred inside.

306
00:18:09,160 --> 00:18:11,120
As for the external wounds,

307
00:18:11,120 --> 00:18:12,880
the extreme internal heat

308
00:18:12,880 --> 00:18:15,280
built pressure that split the skin.

309
00:18:15,640 --> 00:18:17,000
As for the skull,

310
00:18:17,000 --> 00:18:19,320
it shows a heat-induced fracture.

311
00:18:19,320 --> 00:18:21,840
And there was no blood left
for toxicology testing.

312
00:18:30,120 --> 00:18:31,280
I know.

313
00:18:31,280 --> 00:18:33,880
You do care about me, don't you?

314
00:18:34,360 --> 00:18:35,360
Otherwise,

315
00:18:35,720 --> 00:18:38,400
you'd have asked the chief
to send me back to Bangkok.

316
00:18:38,400 --> 00:18:39,360
Get out.

317
00:18:40,360 --> 00:18:41,360
No.

318
00:18:41,360 --> 00:18:43,520
Not until I get every victim's file.

319
00:18:43,520 --> 00:18:44,880
I said get out.

320
00:18:45,640 --> 00:18:47,600
I'll handle this myself.

321
00:18:48,760 --> 00:18:51,920
Afraid I'll solve it first
and embarrass you?

322
00:18:52,200 --> 00:18:54,720
I'm more scared of you wasting my time.

323
00:18:55,200 --> 00:18:57,960
I'll leave once I have all the files.

324
00:18:58,640 --> 00:19:01,440
I believe I've made myself clear,
Inspector Ken.

325
00:19:04,680 --> 00:19:06,040
Fine. I'll send them later.

326
00:19:06,040 --> 00:19:06,840
No need.

327
00:19:07,560 --> 00:19:09,600
What's the harm?

328
00:19:09,600 --> 00:19:11,480
You'll have to work together anyway.

329
00:19:12,120 --> 00:19:13,440
Dr. Ji is right.

330
00:19:19,160 --> 00:19:21,120
Inspector James, come here.

331
00:19:30,680 --> 00:19:32,240
See you, Dr. Ji.

332
00:19:40,760 --> 00:19:41,760
Thanks.

333
00:19:47,320 --> 00:19:49,400
What's this? Where's the evidence?

334
00:19:49,400 --> 00:19:50,720
When did I say I'd give it to you?

335
00:19:50,720 --> 00:19:52,520
Are you messing with me?

336
00:19:52,520 --> 00:19:54,240
Go back to Bangkok. Leave me alone.

337
00:19:56,640 --> 00:19:57,680
I'm not going back

338
00:19:57,680 --> 00:19:59,560
until I find the killer.

339
00:20:00,960 --> 00:20:02,560
You can't go in there.

340
00:20:02,560 --> 00:20:03,480
I said no.

341
00:20:03,480 --> 00:20:05,840
Staff only. You can't enter.

342
00:20:07,680 --> 00:20:08,880
What's going on?

343
00:20:08,880 --> 00:20:10,680
She's the patient's relative.

344
00:20:10,680 --> 00:20:12,560
She wants to see
her daughter-in-law's body.

345
00:20:12,800 --> 00:20:14,720
She says her son didn't burn his wife.

346
00:20:14,720 --> 00:20:17,480
She made this scene when I stopped her.

347
00:20:17,800 --> 00:20:18,760
Hmm.

348
00:20:19,600 --> 00:20:21,040
I'll take it from here.

349
00:20:21,040 --> 00:20:22,200
Thank you.

350
00:20:26,480 --> 00:20:27,760
Hello, ma'am.

351
00:20:28,760 --> 00:20:30,200
Hello.

352
00:20:30,200 --> 00:20:31,080
What did you do now?

353
00:20:31,080 --> 00:20:32,160
Shh.

354
00:20:34,880 --> 00:20:36,720
Please don't lose hope yet, ma'am.

355
00:20:36,960 --> 00:20:38,440
If Joe really is innocent,

356
00:20:38,680 --> 00:20:40,920
we'll find evidence to help him.

357
00:20:42,440 --> 00:20:43,680
Thank you.

358
00:20:45,520 --> 00:20:47,760
But the police are no help at all.

359
00:20:47,960 --> 00:20:49,760
When they can't solve a case,

360
00:20:50,840 --> 00:20:52,520
they blame the Nour ghost.

361
00:20:54,160 --> 00:20:57,960
I only wanted to see the evidence.

362
00:20:58,880 --> 00:21:01,280
They wouldn't let me in either.

363
00:21:02,400 --> 00:21:05,640
I raised my son myself.

364
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:10,360
I know he's a good man.

365
00:21:14,280 --> 00:21:15,720
Don't worry, ma'am.

366
00:21:16,040 --> 00:21:19,320
My team and I will handle this.

367
00:21:19,640 --> 00:21:21,360
Right, partner?

368
00:21:22,720 --> 00:21:24,680
Thank you, Officer.

369
00:21:25,160 --> 00:21:26,680
Thank you so much.

370
00:21:27,960 --> 00:21:30,320
Looks like we're officially
taking this case.

371
00:21:41,240 --> 00:21:44,040
Please save my son.

372
00:21:51,160 --> 00:21:52,560
It'll be okay.

373
00:22:04,760 --> 00:22:05,720
You cripple.

374
00:22:05,720 --> 00:22:07,840
You work one day, then vanish for five.

375
00:22:07,840 --> 00:22:09,840
How long will you mooch off us?

376
00:22:09,840 --> 00:22:12,640
Useless trash. You're a burden.

377
00:22:13,080 --> 00:22:14,160
I'm sorry.

378
00:22:14,480 --> 00:22:16,720
I had a high fever, so I stayed away.

379
00:22:16,720 --> 00:22:18,000
I didn't want to spread my cold.

380
00:22:18,280 --> 00:22:20,240
How dare you talk back?

381
00:22:21,160 --> 00:22:22,560
Look at you. You're a mess.

382
00:22:23,040 --> 00:22:24,400
What a burden.

383
00:22:27,320 --> 00:22:28,320
Chita!

384
00:22:29,600 --> 00:22:30,680
Chita!

385
00:22:33,160 --> 00:22:34,160
Chita!

386
00:22:34,880 --> 00:22:35,640
Chita!

387
00:22:36,000 --> 00:22:37,280
Are you okay?

388
00:22:38,120 --> 00:22:39,280
Here, let me help you.

389
00:22:43,840 --> 00:22:45,040
I'm fine.

390
00:22:47,760 --> 00:22:48,720
I...

391
00:22:49,720 --> 00:22:51,200
should get back to work.

392
00:22:54,560 --> 00:22:56,320
Chita.

393
00:22:57,120 --> 00:22:58,000
I think

394
00:22:58,360 --> 00:23:00,000
you should sit and rest first.

395
00:23:00,440 --> 00:23:01,680
Come on. I'll help you over.

396
00:23:07,920 --> 00:23:08,920
Easy.

397
00:23:11,960 --> 00:23:14,200
How's your leg now?

398
00:23:14,440 --> 00:23:15,760
Let me see.

399
00:23:18,240 --> 00:23:19,360
Excuse me.

400
00:23:34,640 --> 00:23:36,600
It's still the same, Dr. Jirat.

401
00:23:38,560 --> 00:23:40,200
But it's okay.

402
00:23:41,400 --> 00:23:42,480
I'm used to it.

403
00:23:46,960 --> 00:23:49,320
How many times do I have to tell you?
Just call me Dr. Ji.

404
00:23:51,560 --> 00:23:53,680
But your leg seems much better.

405
00:23:58,160 --> 00:23:59,320
It doesn't hurt anymore, right?

406
00:24:01,560 --> 00:24:02,440
It doesn't.

407
00:24:06,280 --> 00:24:08,600
Your current job is too demanding.

408
00:24:12,840 --> 00:24:15,640
There's an opening inside
for a forensic assistant.

409
00:24:23,080 --> 00:24:24,080
Doctor.

410
00:24:24,600 --> 00:24:25,960
You're very kind.

411
00:24:32,760 --> 00:24:33,600
Sorry.

412
00:24:37,480 --> 00:24:40,400
Sit tight for a bit.
Wait for the tightness to ease.

413
00:24:41,680 --> 00:24:42,960
See you tomorrow.

414
00:24:44,800 --> 00:24:45,640
Okay.

415
00:25:10,480 --> 00:25:14,440
(Review of the evidence
and witness statements revealed that...)

416
00:25:20,760 --> 00:25:21,920
(Hey, Inspector.)

417
00:25:22,640 --> 00:25:24,120
Where'd you get my number?

418
00:25:24,840 --> 00:25:26,040
It's a secret.

419
00:25:26,400 --> 00:25:28,520
You have three seconds. One.

420
00:25:28,520 --> 00:25:30,920
(I checked the crime scene evidence.)

421
00:25:30,920 --> 00:25:34,200
Joe couldn't have burned
Somying like that.

422
00:25:34,760 --> 00:25:36,560
But to prove it,

423
00:25:36,560 --> 00:25:38,800
I need more information from you.

424
00:25:38,800 --> 00:25:40,000
Time's up.

425
00:26:02,680 --> 00:26:03,640
Man!

426
00:26:10,320 --> 00:26:12,600
If we wait for you to soften up,

427
00:26:13,600 --> 00:26:15,600
an innocent man will be in prison.

428
00:26:21,240 --> 00:26:24,240
(Joe: Suspect in an arson murder
Somying: Victim, died at the scene)

429
00:26:30,240 --> 00:26:30,960
(Arson Case, Vol. 9)

430
00:26:31,040 --> 00:26:32,840
Arson Case, Volume 9.

431
00:26:33,760 --> 00:26:35,640
Let me see.

432
00:26:41,680 --> 00:26:42,720
(Evidence photos)

433
00:26:58,360 --> 00:27:04,120
(Police Station)

434
00:27:40,160 --> 00:27:43,800
(Evidence photos)

435
00:28:21,960 --> 00:28:28,640
(No Admittance)

436
00:28:41,360 --> 00:28:42,520
Inspector, what are you doing?

437
00:28:45,600 --> 00:28:48,240
You stay on your side.
I'll stay on mine.

438
00:28:48,440 --> 00:28:50,240
We won't interfere with each other.

439
00:28:50,240 --> 00:28:51,320
Show some mutual respect.

440
00:28:57,680 --> 00:28:59,120
This is the first time

441
00:28:59,400 --> 00:29:01,440
you've dared look me in the eye.

442
00:29:03,080 --> 00:29:05,120
What if I don't?

443
00:29:06,440 --> 00:29:08,360
Try me, and I'll pin you down.

444
00:29:12,720 --> 00:29:14,840
You only caught me off guard last time.

445
00:29:15,000 --> 00:29:16,320
I was careless.

446
00:29:23,520 --> 00:29:25,760
Crossing the line isn't a big deal.

447
00:29:31,040 --> 00:29:32,280
But forget it.

448
00:29:32,840 --> 00:29:34,880
I already got everything I needed.

449
00:29:35,800 --> 00:29:39,000
The evidence says something's off too.

450
00:29:39,840 --> 00:29:42,120
Are you hiding something, Inspector?

451
00:29:42,120 --> 00:29:43,840
Why are you so fixated on this case?

452
00:29:44,200 --> 00:29:45,720
What is your relationship to the victim?

453
00:29:46,680 --> 00:29:49,240
Or did you fail to solve
an earlier arson case

454
00:29:49,480 --> 00:29:50,880
and now want to redeem yourself?

455
00:29:53,200 --> 00:29:55,400
What do you know about death?

456
00:29:55,400 --> 00:29:56,640
What gives you the right to say that?

457
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:01,720
More than you do.

458
00:30:02,640 --> 00:30:03,840
So,

459
00:30:04,760 --> 00:30:06,040
don't cross the line.

460
00:30:07,600 --> 00:30:08,760
Same goes for you.

461
00:30:09,080 --> 00:30:10,480
Don't cross mine.

462
00:30:17,880 --> 00:30:19,720
Do we really need to interrogate him?

463
00:30:19,720 --> 00:30:21,480
- Mr. Joe.
- My trial is tomorrow.

464
00:30:21,480 --> 00:30:23,320
What exactly happened that day?

465
00:30:26,160 --> 00:30:27,200
That day...

466
00:30:28,760 --> 00:30:31,880
(Statement Recording)
I went drinking after we argued.

467
00:30:32,120 --> 00:30:33,520
My wife was having an affair.

468
00:30:34,080 --> 00:30:35,200
I was furious.

469
00:30:35,480 --> 00:30:37,000
I came back to confront her.

470
00:30:37,520 --> 00:30:39,240
But when I entered the house...

471
00:30:40,720 --> 00:30:41,680
Fire.

472
00:30:43,640 --> 00:30:45,160
The whole house was on fire.

473
00:30:47,960 --> 00:30:48,840
Nour.

474
00:30:48,840 --> 00:30:49,880
A Nour?

475
00:30:52,440 --> 00:30:54,200
A Nour was choking my wife.

476
00:31:00,520 --> 00:31:01,600
James.

477
00:31:04,360 --> 00:31:05,480
A Nour?

478
00:31:12,480 --> 00:31:13,520
A Nour?

479
00:31:14,320 --> 00:31:16,120
Can you describe it?

480
00:31:16,280 --> 00:31:17,840
What did it look like?

481
00:31:19,320 --> 00:31:21,440
I remember its eyes were blue.

482
00:31:22,960 --> 00:31:24,640
It was choking my wife.

483
00:31:24,640 --> 00:31:25,600
Somying!

484
00:31:26,000 --> 00:31:27,880
I rushed over to save my wife,

485
00:31:27,880 --> 00:31:29,280
but it knocked me unconscious.

486
00:31:30,920 --> 00:31:33,440
I already know what happened.

487
00:31:33,720 --> 00:31:36,120
I'm asking what the killer looked like.

488
00:31:36,960 --> 00:31:38,120
Think carefully.

489
00:31:39,000 --> 00:31:40,560
There must be other details.

490
00:31:43,280 --> 00:31:44,520
I can't remember.

491
00:31:44,520 --> 00:31:45,680
Mr. Joe.

492
00:31:45,680 --> 00:31:47,520
You're the only eyewitness.

493
00:31:47,520 --> 00:31:49,520
How tall was it? What was its build?

494
00:31:49,520 --> 00:31:51,760
Did you see its face?
What else did you notice?

495
00:31:53,360 --> 00:31:55,160
You're pressuring the suspect too much.

496
00:31:55,480 --> 00:31:57,680
That's enough for today.

497
00:32:16,080 --> 00:32:17,560
I'm so nervous.

498
00:32:19,360 --> 00:32:21,760
Well...

499
00:32:22,440 --> 00:32:24,240
Want to rehearse the interview with me?

500
00:32:30,920 --> 00:32:33,440
Why do you want this job,

501
00:32:33,440 --> 00:32:34,400
Chita?

502
00:32:40,000 --> 00:32:42,640
My leg might be a disadvantage,

503
00:32:44,960 --> 00:32:47,040
but I work hard.

504
00:32:48,400 --> 00:32:49,640
So

505
00:32:50,000 --> 00:32:52,160
I never use it as an excuse.

506
00:32:53,280 --> 00:32:54,840
I'm patient,

507
00:32:56,240 --> 00:32:57,840
and I can work well

508
00:32:58,480 --> 00:32:59,880
under pressure.

509
00:33:04,240 --> 00:33:05,920
Then

510
00:33:06,800 --> 00:33:08,240
why should I

511
00:33:08,880 --> 00:33:10,520
choose you over someone else?

512
00:33:16,200 --> 00:33:17,960
I'm used to getting up early.

513
00:33:22,040 --> 00:33:24,320
And I'm not afraid of ghosts.

514
00:33:26,240 --> 00:33:27,360
Not afraid of ghosts?

515
00:33:31,640 --> 00:33:33,160
Okay. You're hired.

516
00:33:34,880 --> 00:33:36,120
What, Doctor?

517
00:33:36,440 --> 00:33:38,120
Get ready. You start today.

518
00:33:41,000 --> 00:33:41,960
That's him.

519
00:33:41,960 --> 00:33:43,040
Yeah.

520
00:33:43,040 --> 00:33:44,520
Is all the paperwork ready?

521
00:33:44,520 --> 00:33:45,240
Yes.

522
00:33:45,880 --> 00:33:48,160
Come inside and fill out the forms.

523
00:33:48,160 --> 00:33:50,880
Finally, someone to help, Dr. Ji.

524
00:33:50,880 --> 00:33:51,760
Come on in.

525
00:33:52,240 --> 00:33:53,240
Doctor.

526
00:33:55,200 --> 00:33:57,840
Weren't we supposed to
have an interview first?

527
00:33:58,280 --> 00:33:59,160
That

528
00:33:59,160 --> 00:34:00,840
was your interview.

529
00:34:01,400 --> 00:34:02,440
Let's go.

530
00:34:04,920 --> 00:34:06,520
Seriously.

531
00:34:06,520 --> 00:34:09,640
All that talk,
no evidence and no killer.

532
00:34:10,360 --> 00:34:12,640
What was that, a ghost story?

533
00:34:14,280 --> 00:34:15,880
But I think Joe told the truth.

534
00:34:16,320 --> 00:34:17,560
Think about it, Officer.

535
00:34:17,920 --> 00:34:19,920
If Joe had killed his wife,

536
00:34:19,920 --> 00:34:21,600
he would've fled long ago.

537
00:34:21,840 --> 00:34:25,040
He wouldn't have caused a scene
demanding justice days ago.

538
00:34:25,600 --> 00:34:27,080
But you have no evidence either

539
00:34:27,080 --> 00:34:29,080
to support that theory.

540
00:34:31,400 --> 00:34:32,640
Hmm.

541
00:34:32,800 --> 00:34:35,200
Let's eat. That's enough for today.

542
00:34:35,360 --> 00:34:36,400
Yeah, let's go.

543
00:34:36,400 --> 00:34:38,320
Let's eat.

544
00:34:40,080 --> 00:34:41,880
How much do you know about the Nour?

545
00:34:46,040 --> 00:34:48,480
You knew about the Nour, didn't you?

546
00:34:57,200 --> 00:34:58,480
What are you doing?

547
00:35:00,200 --> 00:35:02,120
You're hiding something about the Nour.

548
00:35:04,160 --> 00:35:06,080
You reopened a case nearly closed

549
00:35:06,440 --> 00:35:08,400
and believed the suspect's testimony.

550
00:35:08,960 --> 00:35:10,400
What exactly are you digging into?

551
00:35:11,240 --> 00:35:12,440
It just feels suspicious.

552
00:35:12,440 --> 00:35:15,560
I want to know who burned
so many people the same way.

553
00:35:16,320 --> 00:35:18,880
I told you this case isn't for you.

554
00:35:19,320 --> 00:35:21,120
Even if you believe the Nour exists,

555
00:35:22,080 --> 00:35:23,560
Joe isn't the real killer.

556
00:35:23,560 --> 00:35:26,880
Joe will still be arrested tomorrow
for murdering his wife.

557
00:35:26,880 --> 00:35:28,600
You have no choice but to accept it.

558
00:35:30,040 --> 00:35:31,640
I don't believe Nour exists.

559
00:35:32,040 --> 00:35:33,920
But I believe the real killer does.

560
00:35:34,280 --> 00:35:37,080
And I'm sure Joe wasn't lying.

561
00:35:51,280 --> 00:35:53,800
Let me tell you a secret about me.

562
00:35:54,840 --> 00:35:55,680
I...

563
00:35:57,320 --> 00:35:59,760
can spot lies better than a polygraph.

564
00:36:06,440 --> 00:36:09,480
I can usually see right through people.

565
00:36:12,800 --> 00:36:15,400
But no matter how I look at you,

566
00:36:16,640 --> 00:36:18,680
I can never read you.

567
00:36:20,320 --> 00:36:22,960
Are you hiding something from me?

568
00:36:22,960 --> 00:36:24,560
I don't have time for your games.

569
00:36:33,640 --> 00:36:36,480
Thanks for saving me the other day.

570
00:36:36,480 --> 00:36:37,520
You're welcome.

571
00:36:38,280 --> 00:36:41,000
Do you believe the Nour rumors too?

572
00:36:41,480 --> 00:36:43,400
Lately,

573
00:36:43,400 --> 00:36:45,000
it's all strange cases around here.

574
00:36:45,000 --> 00:36:47,240
Even I'm starting to believe them.

575
00:36:50,440 --> 00:36:52,640
Then do you know

576
00:36:52,880 --> 00:36:55,320
who has evidence that could clear Joe?

577
00:36:57,480 --> 00:36:59,320
Probably Inspector Ken.

578
00:36:59,320 --> 00:37:01,040
He's in charge of the case.

579
00:37:01,320 --> 00:37:04,480
Could evidence be stored elsewhere?

580
00:37:06,000 --> 00:37:07,080
Hmm.

581
00:37:07,800 --> 00:37:11,240
It might be in his car.

582
00:37:11,520 --> 00:37:12,560
His car?

583
00:37:49,840 --> 00:37:50,360
(B.E. 2559 Autopsy Report)

584
00:37:55,960 --> 00:37:57,320
(Nour)

585
00:38:06,920 --> 00:38:08,000
Dad.

586
00:38:15,720 --> 00:38:16,600
Dad.

587
00:38:30,880 --> 00:38:31,800
What are you doing?

588
00:38:36,840 --> 00:38:38,440
Inspector, what are you doing?

589
00:39:10,720 --> 00:39:11,600
Did you find it?

590
00:39:12,160 --> 00:39:13,840
What you've been looking for.

591
00:39:23,360 --> 00:39:24,560
(24-hour Self-service Laundry)

592
00:39:24,760 --> 00:39:28,280
(2021 AD, 235th Death)

593
00:40:06,280 --> 00:40:08,000
(Wash, Dry, Iron)

594
00:40:12,400 --> 00:40:13,360
Oh no.

595
00:40:25,600 --> 00:40:26,680
Hey, sir.

596
00:40:26,680 --> 00:40:28,200
Sir?

597
00:40:28,560 --> 00:40:29,240
Sir?

598
00:40:29,480 --> 00:40:30,120
Sir?

599
00:41:10,440 --> 00:41:11,560
Come here.

600
00:41:11,920 --> 00:41:12,800
Sit down first.

601
00:41:29,520 --> 00:41:30,320
Here.

602
00:41:30,680 --> 00:41:32,080
Dry your hair.

603
00:41:32,480 --> 00:41:34,760
If you get sick and die,

604
00:41:35,040 --> 00:41:36,560
I don't want that bad luck.

605
00:41:50,760 --> 00:41:51,560
It stinks.

606
00:41:52,160 --> 00:41:53,080
What?

607
00:41:53,360 --> 00:41:54,480
Sorry.

608
00:41:54,920 --> 00:41:57,040
I just used that on cat pee.

609
00:41:58,720 --> 00:41:59,440
Hmm.

610
00:41:59,960 --> 00:42:01,200
This one should work.

611
00:42:16,240 --> 00:42:17,640
What's wrong with you?

612
00:42:17,640 --> 00:42:18,960
Did someone dump you?

613
00:42:19,360 --> 00:42:21,720
But you're so handsome.

614
00:42:21,720 --> 00:42:23,920
You'll find a new lover soon.

615
00:42:23,920 --> 00:42:24,880
Don't overthink it.

616
00:42:25,240 --> 00:42:27,160
If you need someone to talk to,

617
00:42:27,160 --> 00:42:29,720
call the 1323 mental health hotline.

618
00:42:29,720 --> 00:42:31,520
Or you may...

619
00:42:32,960 --> 00:42:33,760
Hey!

620
00:42:38,920 --> 00:42:40,080
Hey, sir!

621
00:42:40,920 --> 00:42:42,760
I'll be here for another hour.

622
00:42:43,720 --> 00:42:45,000
If you change your mind,

623
00:42:45,360 --> 00:42:46,680
you can come back.

624
00:42:48,120 --> 00:42:49,400
What a strange guy.
